      madhyamaka: 'Garfield: this verse introduces the identity/difference analysis (na ekam na pṛthak) that Nāgārjuna employs throughout the MMK (cf. Ch.10 fire-fuel, Ch.18 self-aggregates, Ch.22 Tathāgata-aggregates). Kalupahana: the verse instantiates the Middle Way — avoiding the extreme of identity (eternalism/one-ness) and the extreme of difference (annihilationism/total separation). Candrakīrti: if identical, agent and action collapse; if different, they become unrelated.',
      quantum: 'Entanglement / Non-Separability: Entangled particles are neither identical (they can have different locations, spins) nor completely independent (measuring one instantly constrains the other). Their relationship transcends the classical identity/difference binary — they are non-separable without being the same.',
