      madhyamaka: 'Garfield: "non-existent" (avidyamāna) means lacking svabhāva, NOT conventionally non-existent. Motion happens — people walk, cars drive — but none of these have inherent existence. Kalupahana: the addition of "route" (adhvan) is significant — even the PATH of motion is empty, completing the trinity of agent, action, and locus. Candrakīrti: this verse is the mahāsiddhi (great accomplishment) of Ch. 2 — the complete demonstration that motion in all its aspects is empty.',
      quantum: 'Emergent Actuality / Contextual Properties: Quantum properties don\'t pre-exist measurement — they emerge contextually. Position, momentum, spin are not "there" waiting to be found; they arise through interaction with measurement apparatus. All three elements of quantum measurement (system, property, apparatus) are relationally constituted, not inherently fixed.',
